        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dil_ninja/{size}/5218_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-09-24T10:01:51.851Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Having played them all through once, I’m in agreement with Churro’s ratings.</p>\n<p>I’d say the War-Girded Fey Court are much easier than the base version. No weighing the benefits of what minions to keep for tokens, just kill 'em all. And once you deal with the setup wave, they usually just play 1 weak minion a turn for the rest of the game. There’s also not much reason to mess with the bonds if you’re not playing on Advanced.</p>",
